      "name": "Commercial Move Operations",
      "description": "Commercial move operations for business relocations, planned around the operation. The published hero framing is verbatim: Business moves, planned around your operation. Commercial relocations are quoted flat and agreed in writing before move day, planned around the hours, the site, and the equipment, with the warehouse and transload operation behind the job. The operation chain runs survey, quote, phased plan, pack and label, sequenced move, install and place, verify, and close-out, with a plan core of what moves first, what moves last, and what works on day one. Survey runs through the quote form Short (Quick Quote) default and Detailed Project toggle with inputs preserved, and a film-only video walkthrough where a walkthrough fits: film only, never lift, move, open, or climb anything heavy or locked, with a human-made estimate. The freight chain is container loading and unloading, transloading, and final-mile delivery; high-mass or sensitive devices to 3,500 lbs ride the SIR and KIM-GS method conditionally, with floor deflection analysis to L/360. Shops, professional offices, and commercial spaces are the published audience; industrial offices, government offices, and military households are cross-references to their own categories, never duplicated here. Commercial relocations are planned as a single coordinated operation: survey, phased plan, pack and label, sequenced move, install and place, verify, and close-out, with the plan core of what moves first, what moves last, and what works on day one. Scope, phasing, and price are agreed in writing before move day.",
